      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is the process where one cell divides into two identical daughter cells, which is crucial for growth and repair in living things. This process allows organisms to effectively learn and grow by duplicating their genetic material perfectly. By following the distinct phases—prophase, metaphase, anaphase, and telophase—students can easily understand how the cell divides to create two identical copies. This clear breakdown will help students learn the core concepts of cell division.",
